  "generated_text": "1. **Calculate the side length of region I:**\n   Since the perimeter of region I is 12 units, each side of the square is $\\frac{12}{4} = 3$ units.\n\n2. **Calculate the area of region I:**\n   The area of region I is $3^{2} = 9$ square units.\n\n3. **Calculate the side length of region II:**\n   Since the perimeter of region II is 24 units, each side of the square is $\\frac{24}{4} = 6$ units.\n\n4. **Calculate the area of region II:**\n   The area of region II is $6^{2} = 36$ square units.\n\n5. **Calculate the area of region III:**\n   Since region III is the same as region II, its area is also $36$ square units.\n\n6. **Calculate the ratio of the area of region I to the area of region III:**\n   The ratio is $\\frac{9}{36} = \\frac{1}{4}$.\n\n7. **Conclusion:** The ratio of the area of region I to the area of region III is $\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}$.",
  "grade": {
